# ── Rust build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
**/target/
debug/
**/debug/

# Compiled libraries and objects
**/*.rlib
**/*.rmeta
**/*.d
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/*.pdb

# Shared / dynamic libraries
**/*.so
**/*.so.*
**/*.dylib
**/*.dll

# Z3 solver debug trace (written to cwd by bahyway-z3's dev-time-only tests)
.z3-trace

# Godot import/editor cache (generated per-machine by the engine, incl. PB-227's
# headless --import priming pass -- never hand-authored, never committed)
**/.godot/

# Executables and binaries
**/*.exe
**/*.out

# Incremental compilation state
**/incremental/
**/.fingerprint/
**/build/

# Rustfmt backup files
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo mutation testing output
**/mutants.out*/

# ── WASM / trunk build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
**/dist/
pkg/
**/pkg/
*.wasm

# ── IDE / editor state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/settings.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/tasks.json
.vscode/*.log
!.vscode/extensions.json

.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

.zed/

# DubSar IDE runtime state
*.dubsar-session
*.dubsar-cache

# ── OS-generated files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ── Logs and reports ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
*.report
*.log.gz

# ── Temporary / swap files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig

# ── Secrets and environment files ────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.cert

# ── Benchmark / profiling artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────
criterion/
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# ── Coverage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
lcov.info
coverage/
tarpaulin-report.html

# ── IsimudEngine generated reports (regenerated every run — not source) ──
# `docs/SHEDU/*` (not `docs/SHEDU/`) is deliberate: a directory-level
# pattern with a trailing slash prunes the whole directory from
# traversal, so a later `!docs/SHEDU/specific_file.md` negation is
# silently never evaluated (confirmed live via `git check-ignore -v` --
# both a generated report AND an intended exception matched the same
# directory rule). The `*` form still ignores every file by default but
# keeps per-file negation below actually working.
docs/SHEDU/*
# Exceptions: authored content that happens to live in this directory,
# not orchestrator run-output -- tracked deliberately, 2026-07-26.
!docs/SHEDU/DEPLOY_REFERENCE_ALL_PLAYBOOKS.md
!docs/SHEDU/GLOSSARY_ADDENDUM_2026-07-25.md
!docs/SHEDU/NARU_AUDIT_JOURNAL.md
!docs/SHEDU/NISABA_KITTU_SECURITY_INTERFACE_2026-07-25.md
!docs/SHEDU/RM-001_ADDENDUM_PB111-145_RECONCILED_V2_2026-07-26.md
